# 5. Mathematical Intuition

DBSCAN is based on the concept of an **epsilon neighborhood**.

For a point \(p\):

\[
N_{\epsilon}(p)
=
\{q \mid d(p,q)\leq\epsilon\}
\]

This means:

> Find all points within distance `eps` of point \(p\).

A point is considered a **core point** when its neighborhood satisfies the required minimum density.

---

# 6. DBSCAN vs K-Means ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐

| Feature | K-Means | DBSCAN |
|---|---|---|
| Need number of clusters? | Yes, \(K\) | No |
| Cluster shape | Best for compact/spherical patterns | Can handle arbitrary shapes |
| Outlier detection | Weak | Strong |
| Uses centroids | Yes | No |
| Main parameters | K | `eps`, `min_samples` |
| Initialization sensitive | Yes | Generally not in the same way |
| Different densities | Can struggle | Can also struggle when densities vary greatly |

