# 7. Why DBSCAN Handles Arbitrary Shapes

Consider moon-shaped clusters:

```text
🌙 🌙 🌙

      🌙 🌙 🌙
```

K-Means tries to divide data based on distance to centroids.

DBSCAN instead follows:

> **Density connections**

If points form a continuous dense chain, DBSCAN can connect them into the same cluster.

This makes it useful for:

- Geographic data
- Spatial patterns
- Complex natural clusters

