# 21. Explain to an Interviewer — 60-Second Script 🎤

> DBSCAN is an unsupervised density-based clustering algorithm. It groups together data points located in dense regions and labels isolated points as noise. Its two main parameters are epsilon, which defines the neighborhood radius, and min_samples, which defines the density required for a core point. DBSCAN can discover arbitrarily shaped clusters and does not require specifying the number of clusters beforehand. However, it is sensitive to parameter selection and can struggle when clusters have significantly different densities or when data is high-dimensional.

