Answer:

> **Why can DBSCAN initially mark a point as noise, but later include it in a cluster?**

### Ideal Answer:

> When first visited, a point may not belong to a sufficiently dense region and can be temporarily labeled as noise. Later, if the algorithm discovers that the point lies within the neighborhood of a core point, it can become a border point and be assigned to that cluster.

